cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or benchmark, please cite this release."
title: "dense-solver: A pigeonhole SAT benchmark"
type: software
version: "0.0.2"
authors:
  - given-names: Merlin
    family-names: Numa
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/libdense/dense-solver"
abstract: >-
  A C SAT solver and a reproducible single-core benchmark of the pigeonhole
  principle. The release includes pairwise and sequential-counter DIMACS inputs,
  native source, a reusable counting pass, a local browser interface and individual timings. Merlin Numa
  directed the work using OpenAI ChatGPT and Anthropic Claude through paid
  subscriptions.
keywords:
  - Boolean satisfiability
  - pigeonhole principle
  - cardinality constraints
  - SAT solver
  - reproducible benchmarking

references:
